laws bc_sat_areab_only sub_sat_emission_ns diode_wl_mult_once diode_sidewall_own_f1 diode_xom_absent_1e14 vdmos_kp_absent_20 vdmos_tcvth_raises vdmos_clamp_by_fc mos_small_signal_exact mos6_small_signal_exact bjt_irb_small_signal_exact vdmos_mult_charges_copies diode_isr_reverse_present diode_isr_small_signal_exact diode_tt_factor_clamped trig_exact exp_exact log_zero_error div_exact asin_edge_fails
# Oracle: VD cmd-save (directives accumulate; default, v(), i(), p(inst, var), hierarchical
# names quoted); run e5 (`default` holds every node voltage and every branch current, an
# inductor's included: all_v + all_branch_i; `save v(b)` governs op, its sweeps and tran, not
# ac; `full` is every unknown, internal nodes included: Private, P2308); `dv` is the ac's own
# directive, which no probe kind states (P2308); `clear saves` drops every save before it (run sv2: a Reset of the saves, A27);
# a save holds from where it stands (runs sv1, sv2).
# A22: the set of kinds a line governs is stated exactly (op, its sweeps, tran; with `default`
# and no p() also ac and dcinc, whose own directive `default` is).
# codes: P2308 P2308 S0002 S0002
file "save.sim" deck
  title "save directives"
  save analysis=(op dc tran) from_here (all_v) (all_branch_i) (v (a)) (i (v1)) (param (r1) (i)) (v (x1 n))
  opaque vacask private "save full"
  opaque vacask private "save dv(a)"
  reset saves
